 "notes": [
  "Step 1 change: added wire6 (a sixth jumper wire). It carries 5V from the top rail to the button's supply side, which is on the bottom half of the breadboard across the centre gap. Step 1 had assumed 5 wires, and the page gives no wire count.",
  "Wiring follows the schematic. Each photoresistor goes from 5V to its analog pin (A0 or A1), and a 10k resistor goes from that pin to GND, as a voltage divider.",
  "The pushbutton's side 1 (top half) goes to pin 2, with a 10k pull-down to GND on the same side. Its side 2 (bottom half) goes to 5V.",
  "The top rail 'tp' is 5V and 'tn' is GND. Component legs are put straight into rail holes, since the circuit images did not show an exact breadboard layout. Hole positions are my choice.",
  "Sensors are photoresistors because the schematic draws them as photocells. A potentiometer or FSR would work too, as the parts list says."
 ],
